  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-1",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "I always tell people looking at Datadog to remember \"DDDD\" or \"DataDog Don't Discount\". Compared to most Enterprise vendors it is a lot harder to get a discount from Datadog.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-2",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "We spend a few thousand a month with Datadog and our account manager reaches out every quarter to adjust our monthly commit up/down which provides a 20% discount off from the website prices.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-3",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "Their main competitive advantage is being able to correlate data across APM, custom metrics, and logging through the use of tagging, densely linking data together across the platform, including built-in Jupyter-style notebooks.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-4",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "I wish Datadog was just opinionated as hell and said everything you see is UTC by default... It's insane that software designed to help people unfuck production systems doesn't display timezone by default.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-5",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "Their data correlation is awful compared to competitors like Honeycomb, Dynatrace and Instana. We shouldn't be sifting through a bunch of outdated dashboards and notebooks in this day and age.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-6",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/42648043",
    "excerpt": "DD was just easier to use for everybody, has lots of useful baked-in things we liked to use (apdex scores), and was intuitive enough that non-devs could design their own dashboards. We also found it way easier to collect metrics, traces, and other things.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-7",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/42648043",
    "excerpt": "Datadog lost our business for two reasons: 1) Lack of billing transparency and 2) an incompetent account rep who managed to piss off our finance department while also embarrassing our CTO. Our spend was over $6M/yr with Datadog... we'll never go back.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-8",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/42648043",
    "excerpt": "We switched from Datadog to Grafana (do not recommend unless they got you over a barrel on pricing and you need to escape).",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-9",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=20781610",
    "excerpt": "I had bad experiences with them - difficulty with setup and tracking ability, including a much more resource intensive approach than newrelic for collecting execution traces. Emails went unanswered until a co-worker reached out publicly on Twitter.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-10",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=20781610",
    "excerpt": "As a long time customer, I can attest that they thoroughly deserve their success. Their product has always been amazing. Absolutely reliable. Beautifully well designed. We never once flinched at our bill.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-11",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=20781610",
    "excerpt": "As a user, I can say Datadog solves a real (and burning) problem for product engineering teams, and, though expensive, is worth every penny.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-12",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=33049046",
    "excerpt": "I don't know what other people's experience has been with DataDog, but the user interface experience I had with it was definitely reminiscent of something produced from a dog's rear end. Definitely a product where no one in the org said 'no' to an idea.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-13",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=33049046",
    "excerpt": "I like DataDog but it is prohibitively expensive for monitoring serverless applications, even with negotiated rates... Paying for DataDog is many orders of magnitude higher than our AWS bill.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-14",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "If you want my two Datadog favourite features, they were: 1) clicking on a field and making it a custom search dimension in another click, and 2) flame graphs. Delicious flame graphs.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-15",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "This is awesome! Datadog's one of my favorite providers, and their pricing is great for small businesses, but probably unaffordable for larger businesses.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-16",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "I'm interested. Datadog is cool but the price is ridiculously high for small orgs.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-17",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "Datadog's server hexagon map/chart thingie is something else. The kind of innovation that wins prizes.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T01:08:51.426Z"
  },
